[0.000, "o", "\u001b[1m5. Local API (lexicon serve)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m   skipped (--no-serve)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[1m6. Dictation app\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.009, "o", "   wrote ~/Desktop/lexicon-macos.plist (122 terms)\r\n   import it in System Settings > Keyboard > Text Replacements (drag the file in)\r\n\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[1m7. Does it work?\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.013, "o", "   you dictate:  can you ask Mason Wiatt where the Ashler migration landed\r\n   \u001b[1myour agent sees\u001b[0m: \u001b[1mcan you ask Mason Wyatt where the Ashlr.AI migration landed\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m   fixed: \"Mason Wiatt\" -> \"Mason Wyatt\", \"Ashler\" -> \"Ashlr.AI\"\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1mDone.\u001b[0m\r\n   lexicon: ~/.config/lexicon/lexicon.yaml\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "   terms added: Mason Wyatt, Ashlr.AI\r\n   packs: developer (70 added), ai (36 added), voice-tools (14 added)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "   clients: claude, codex, cursor, claude-desktop, vscode\r\n   local API: skipped\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "   exports: ~/Desktop/lexicon-macos.plist\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1mNext:\u001b[0m open Claude Code and dictate a sentence with \"Ashlr.AI\" in it. That is the whole thing.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[2m   later: lexicon suggest (names you keep correcting), lexicon stats, lexicon voice (local push-to-talk)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
